3. blocking — brief:82,122 — The agent-written whole-header sticky rule makes an unusually long title a permanent obstruction. In `drawer-many-390.png`, the header occupies approximately 390px of the 852px drawer; pinning it sacrifices nearly half the reading area throughout detail scrolling. — replace with: At 390px, keep only the existing 44px Close control pinned, with an opaque backing and visible focus indicator. Let the complete title, metadata and remaining detail scroll in their existing order; neither truncate the title nor add a toolbar. — check: `apps/web/tests-serve/w411.spec.ts`, b3: the long-title header scrolls away while Close remains reachable and record content remains readable through the bottom.

